WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.380
Thor: Love and Thunder, the fourth Thor solo
flick is scheduled to rocket into theaters

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.460
on November 5th, 2021.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.880
That's more than enough to send fans racing
to mark their calendars, but a major question

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.340
remained after Marvel Studios announced Love
and Thunder's release date.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.440
We know when it's coming to the big screen,
but when does it take place in the Marvel

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.660
Cinematic Universe?

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.120
Thor is a little flighty when it comes to
keeping track of time, afterall.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:24.780
"He's gonna come back."

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.920
"Except, you know, last time he was gone for
like… two years…"

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.500
Thanks to Marvel luminary James Gunn, who
was not long ago reinstated as the writer

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.900
and director of Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.
3, we have an answer.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.120
In the comments section of his recent Instagram
post congratulating Avengers: Endgame on beating

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:49.800
Avatar at the box office, Gunn fielded a question
about Thor: Love and Thunder's place in the

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.160
MCU in relation to Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 3.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:58.200
A fan inquired whether Love and Thunder will
be set before or after the new Guardians flick,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.960
and Gunn gave a simple, one-word answer: "Before."

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.060
Gunn's response was clear - the fourth Thor
comes before the third Guardians - but it

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.240
opens up a whole can of worms and invites
a lot of speculation.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.200
The last we saw of the God of Thunder was
at the end of Avengers: Endgame, where he

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.820
was sporting a brand-new physique and a renewed
interpretation of what it means to be a superhero,

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.200
handing the kingship of New Asgard over to
Valkyrie, and teaming up with the Guardians

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.180
of the Galaxy gang.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:28.900
Now, Marvel filmmakers and screenwriters basically
never do anything without serious forethought.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:32.910
It's for this reason that we can imagine Thor
and the Guardians will be together at least

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:36.540
at the start of Thor: Love and Thunder to
pick up from where their story left off in

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:40.810
Endgame — exactly like how the events of
Avengers: Infinity War started mere moments

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.020
after the action of Thor: Ragnarok ended.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.060
"I feel like everything's going to work out
fine."

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.480
Gunn's confirmation of when in the MCU Thor:
Love and Thunder takes place unfortunately

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.720
doesn't address when Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 3 will debut in theaters.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:05.240
Prior to the Walt Disney Company booting him
from the film after unsavory past tweets of

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:09.759
his surfaced, Gunn was planning for the next
entry in his franchise to premiere sometime

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.580
in 2020.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.680
Plans changed after he was fired, when Warner
Bros. and DC Films poached Gunn to write and

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.380
direct The Suicide Squad, a reboot-slash-sequel
to David Ayer's Suicide Squad.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.860
As we all know, the House of Mouse eventually
changed its tune and tapped Gunn to come back

00:02:24.871 --> 00:02:28.989
on board - but by then, Gunn was committed
to a different movie in a totally different

00:02:28.989 --> 00:02:30.500
comic book film franchise.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:34.840
Gunn has since stated that he'll finish The
Suicide Squad before starting production on

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:40.860
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, so that previously
projected 2020 release date is no longer valid.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.140
Neither are those past predictions that Guardians
3 would be a Phase 4 movie.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:50.720
At San Diego Comic-Con 2019, Marvel dropped
a slate of five movies and five television

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:56.630
shows arriving in 2020 and 2021, which studio
head Kevin Feige has said is the "complete"

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.040
Phase 4 for the time being.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:02.340
There's no sign of Guardians on that slate,
which seems to mean that the next time we

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:08.460
see the Guardians trying to save the galaxy,
it'll be in Phase 5, probably in 2022 or 2023.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:13.120
There are still some lingering questions when
it comes to Thor: Love and Thunder and Guardians

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.569
of the Galaxy Vol. 3, but we know two things
for sure: Love and Thunder will bring us Natalie

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:21.750
Portman's Jane Foster as Mighty Thor, and
will introduce Valkyrie as the first openly

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.900
LGBTQ+ superhero in the MCU.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:29.360
It may or may not have the Guardians of the
Galaxy in it, but Love and Thunder is definitely

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.040
going to be both lovely and thunderously fun.

